{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1462294-stuck-on-siskur-dah-and-craving-input","id":1462294,"title":"Stuck on Siskur-Dah and craving input","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-01T11:06:30-07:00","id":1462294,"title":"Stuck on Siskur-Dah and craving input","content":"Hi all, <br /> <br /> Brand new to the forum. I'm having trouble zeroing in on Siskur-Dah and how to use it. If I'm in the wrong spot, all apologies and feel free to redirect me.<br /> <br /> First: In using Sister-Dah to replenish essence, how exactly does that take place? The rules say that when you kill a spirit while the rite is invoked you may divide its remaining essence amongst the pack. What is meant by killing or bringing a spirit down? destroying its Corpus? In the spirit combat rules it states that destroying a spirit and draining its essence kills it permanently. It also says that killing spirits permanently is a matter of some gravity not to be done often or without good reason. <i>How do you kill a spirit properly in accordance with the laws of the Hisil and then drain its essence without discorporating it thus killing it forever? What does the look like? </i><br /> <br /> Furthermore, if the process <i>is</i> some version of hunt it down discorporate it and then drink the left over magic smoke, then doesn't that kind of mess up the idea of spiritual hunters tearing apart their prey? It seems like hunting spirits in the shadow would be where the act was most essentially wolf-like and predatory. However if I'm reading the rules as written correctly it seem like spiritual combat and predation of spirits is the least visceral and animalistic which doesn't jive for me. <br /> <br /> I'm super enthusiastic about the game and have wanted to play since I was a kid and had the Apocalypse books. I'm really excited to hear what anyone has to say about how to make these concepts gel better in my mind so I can translate them in a satisfying and interesting way to my group. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27109-lawrence-kessler","name":"Lawrence Kessler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27109_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T11:30:45-07:00","id":1462300,"title":"","content":"Away from my books and thus working from memory, but: You can take less than the spirit's entire stock of Essence, thus allowing it to reform later, and it's completely consuming its reserves that kills it utterly and is frowned upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T14:05:00-07:00","id":1462320,"title":"","content":"Descriptively you don't &quot;eat smoke&quot;, you do eat the &quot;flesh&quot; of the spirit as a representation of its essence. But as long as you don't consume all the essence the spirit will reform, kind of how Thor's goats reform in &quot;Norse&quot; Mythology.<br /> <br /> But it is also important to remember that Uratha, the werewolves from Forsaken, <i>aren't wolves</i>. They're wolf <i>spirits</i>. The difference is extremely important and many things that apply to wolves may not apply to them.<br /> <br /> Even then, yes, they are savage in the Shadow, but not savage as wolves, savage as spirits. And it frequently include destroying other spirits, but also avoiding destruction of your source of meals. It also involves strange behaviors as spirits have Bans and ritualistic behaviors by nature. Forsaken have a very distinct vibe from Apocalypse in this regard, as werewolves are less shamanistic and more spirit proper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T17:19:52-07:00","id":1462361,"title":"","content":"If you\u2019re just fighting a spirit without the Sacred Hunt, you don\u2019t get to drain its Essence. It can use its Essence, and some abilities may force it to use its Essence, but that\u2019s a resource the spirit has, not the Uratha. If the werewolves injure the spirit down to 0 Corpus (from lethal or aggravated) and it still has Essence available, the spirit dissipates but will reform somewhere else, eventually. The werewolves get no more than temporarily eliminating a threat, but it may be back some day. If the spirit has exhausted its Essence and you reduce its Corpus to 0, it dies. The Uratha may have the sense of a job well done, but that\u2019s it. (Side note: Spirits know they die at 0 Corpus, 0 Essence. If a Spirit is under attack it\u2019s most likely going to try to flee if one or the other gets too low.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Being under the Siskur-dah changes the rules of the hunt. Now, the spirit is bound within ancient bonds and things work a little differently. If the Uratha get it to 0 Corpus, the spirit doesn\u2019t just immediately dissipate. The werewolves have some options. They can take any remaining Essence from the spirit for themselves and permit it to dissipate - the spirit goes away, more drained than ever before, but knowing that the werewolves spared its life. It knows that they could have chosen otherwise, which may have an impact on the spirit. The werewolves can choose to destroy the spirit as they divide its Essence, and may do so if they figure that\u2019s the better long-term course. The werewolves also have a third choice - if the spirit knows a Gift they want (and they have Experience to spend), they can instead force the spirit to mark their flesh and give them the Gift in exchange for its life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T08:38:46-07:00","id":1462428,"title":"","content":"Oh I see now. Ha ha that answers my question so thoroughly all I can say now is thank you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27109-lawrence-kessler","name":"Lawrence Kessler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27109_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}